<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka Tobacco interim net up 19 pct.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka Tobacco interim net up 19 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unaudited results for the six months ended June 30, 1996:</p>
<p>(in millions of rupees unless stated):</p>
<p>				  H1 1996	    H1 1995</p>
<p>    Turnover		 8,391.15   vs    8,002.12</p>
<p>    Net profit		 230.87   vs	194.18</p>
<p>    Tax provision	    127.46   vs	134.94</p>
<p>NOTE - Ceylon Tobacco Company Ltd, Sri Lanka's monopoly cigarette maker, is a subsidiary of B.A.T Industries Plc.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
